l. Same clipped common normalized hourly return; no refit or new feature.","comparisons":"Adaptive versus fixed-shrunk base, unshrunk, earlier adjusted temperature, frozen flow and neutral. All comparisons also test past frequency. Preserve original all-anchor52% direction gate.","motivation":"Sequential follow-up after prequential temperature correction worsened Brier versus the unpenalized model in8/9 cohorts. Hypothesis: directly shrinking the raw common-hour coefficient avoids an extra time-varying calibration scale. Not proof that scale drift caused the previous loss.","primary":"Calibration success requires all9 conditional information gates vs base AND unshrunk AND neutral. General solution also requires all9 vs flow and all9 original adaptive direction gates. Conditional thresholds unchanged: accuracy lower99.444%>50%, Brier/logloss gain lower99.444%>0 vs named control and frequency,>=5 positive monthly Brier gains,>=100 each direction. Earlier-temperature comparison diagnostic.","protected":"No market sources/outcomes from2026-08-01 onward. Reuse frozen data and models; preserve every previous result. No downloads, installs, orders or profitability claim.","purpose":"Correct excessive fixed shrinkage using measured uncertainty of the single common-hour coefficient; no second temperature factor.","scope":"All550362 original anchors, five-minute spot target anchor+60sec to anchor+360sec, unchanged flat probabilities. Positive beta preserves original up/down decisions, zero means neutral. No asset-specific calibration or new optimized scalar.","status":"Retrospective Jan-Jul2024/2025/2026 BTC/ETH/SOL. Outcomes and earlier fitted coefficients already explored; no pristine or prospective claim.","uncertainty":"Frozen4000 paired7day blocks seed271032,9cohort correction per endpoint, no joint correction across endpoints/comparisons/sequential research history. Same fixed reliability bins as temperature study; ECE/gaps descriptive. No bootstrap refitting."}}
